  "summary": "Only externally CFO-assisted positive maps pass the existing combined detector gate; all three positive assisted individual maps also pass as observations. This supports a recorded-data candidate, not a unique frame origin or a locked timing bound. The winning drift is the bank edge and follows different ambiguity lobes across maps.",
  "numerical_method": {
    "saved_maps": "Exactly3x20000 uint16 little-endian values. Widen to signed64 before arithmetic. For each ORIGINAL drift d in[-12,-8,-4,0,4,8,12], combined[p]=sum(map[i,(p+i*d)%20000]); argmax uses first tie. Median/MAD from that combined map; z=(max-median)/(1.4826*MAD). No new hypotheses or altered gates.",
    "rank": "One plus number of strictly larger values in a map; ties share rank.",
    "glrt_fit": "Use every31 saved positive window integer epoch, phase_us=((3*epoch)%100000)/75; fit np.polyfit((window_start-first_window_start)/25e6,phase_us,1). Phase does not cross a modulo boundary here. Overlapping windows violate independence; this is descriptive, not a confidence interval or calibrated clock estimate.",
    "same_tile_reference": "Only saved20ms windows whose complete support lies inside each64-frame map score interval; compare map maximum to median saved epoch phase. This is not a per-frame timing error distribution.",
    "autocorrelation": "Frozen projected_pss(15000000,upper), complex128 direct full autocorrelation, squared magnitude divided by zero-lag squared magnitude. These deterministic sidelobes alone do not prove the cause of real-capture lobe selection."
  },
